2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonso_I_de_Portugal
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso I of Portugal (Portuguese: Afonso Henriques; Guimarães or Viseo, July 25, 1109b - Coimbra, December 6, 1185),3 was the second count of the Portucalense County of the house of Burgundy and the first king of Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT The extramarital offspring by Elvira Gálter were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Urraca Alfonso.41 In 1185 his father donated Avô to him. In the donation it stipulates that the lordship could only pass to the children had with her husband Pedro Alfonso de Ribadouro (also called Pedro Alfonso Viegas) grandson
2 CONC  of Egas Moniz, "el Ayo."42 which may indicate another marriage, before or after being widowed to Pedro Alfonso. In 1187 he changed this lordship of Avô to that of Aveiro with his half-brother, King Sancho I of Portugal. He died a
2 CONC fter 1216 since in January of that year the couple made a donation to the monastery of Tarouca.43 A daughter of Urraca and her husband Pedro Alfonso de Ribadouro was Sancha Pérez de Lumiares who married Pedro Rodríguez Girón.44
2 CONT * Teresa Alfonso (1135-?), in some genealogies she appears as the daughter of Elvira Gálter,45 and in others as the daughter of Chamoa Gómez. He first married Sancho Núñez de Barbosa from whom he had Urraca Sánchez, the wife of Go
2 CONC nzalo Méndez de Sousa, father of Count Mendo González de Sousa called the "Sousaõ".46 Then he remarried the rich man Fernando Martins Bravo, lord of Braganza and Chávez from whom he had no succession.46
2 CONT
2 CONT Fonte: https://arquivos.azores.gov.pt/viewer?id=1351578&FileID=2291&recordType=Description
2 CONT
