0 @N6000000002187721147@ NOTE Henry of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry of Burgundy (1035 – ca.1074) was the son and heir of Robert I, duke of Burgundy. He died shortly before his father and failed to succeed in Burgundy. He married Sibylle of Barcelona (ca. 1035- July 6, 1074), daughter of Bere
1 CONC nger Ramon I of Barcelona, and their children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh I, Duke of Burgundy (1057-1093) 
1 CONT Eudes I, Duke of Burgundy (1058-1103) 
1 CONT Robert, bishop of Langres (1059-1111) 
1 CONT Helie, a nun (b.1061) 
1 CONT Beatrice (b.1063), married Guy I, count of Vignory 
1 CONT Renauld, abbot of St Pierre (1065-1092) 
1 CONT Henry, Count of Portugal (1066-1112), who became a vassal of Castile and ruler of the county of Portugal in 1093; his son would be Alfonso Henriques, first king of Portugal 
0 @N6000000000437107474@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Duke Name Suffix:<NSFX> I, of Burgundy
0 @N6000000002247926813@ NOTE died d.v.p.(died during his father's lifetime)
